# Archived pre-2.0 code, kept on disk but out of the repo
Old Calendar Files/

# Build artifacts / distributables — the plugin ships as source, not a zip
*.zip

# Partial downloads
*.crdownload

# Per-developer Claude Code overrides. Every "always allow" click during a
# session is appended here, so it grows into a long unreviewed list that is
# personal to one machine. .claude/settings.json is the curated, committed
# file; this one is deliberately not shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Working notes, transcripts and handover documents dropped in the project
# root. These are not part of the plugin and must never be committed — one of
# them turned out to contain a live credential and had to be scrubbed from
# history. Patterns are deliberately broad and case-insensitive by duplication,
# because the cost of a stray note being ignored is nil and the cost of one
# being committed is a history rewrite.
*[Tt]ranscript*
*TRANSCRIPT*
*[Cc]hat[Ll]og*
*[Cc]hat-[Ll]og*
*[Hh]andover*.txt
*[Hh]andoff*
*[Ss]ession[-_ ]*.txt
*[Nn]otes.txt
*[Ss]cratch*.txt
*.transcript
/*.log

# The Events Calendar exports, dropped in the project root for the one-time
# import. Four WXR files, 5MB, holding a whole site's event history including
# trashed and draft rows and the addresses and phone numbers of staff. What the
# import actually uses is committed, extracted and byte-exact, in
# .claude/import/plan.php. These stay on disk and out of the repository.
SFAF Calendar Export.xml
series.xml
organizadores.xml
recintos.xml

# Source documents for the import, dropped in the project root: the Stonewall
# Project group info sheet and anything that follows it. Same reasoning as the
# exports. What the import uses is in .claude/import/plan.php.
Event Documents/

# GoFundMe Pro's own OpenAPI spec, 2.2 MB. Kept on disk because two comments
# in class-sfaf-source-gfmp.php and PROJECT.md cite it as the source of truth
# for the endpoint and the Campaign schema, and out of the repository because it
# is their document, carries no licence granting redistribution, and is a third
# of the repository's weight. Re-download it from their developer docs.
apiv2-public-gfmp.json

# Anything under a folder explicitly marked private/local.
private/
scratch/
_local/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*~

# The staging tree build-zip.sh assembles. Rebuilt on every build.
.build-stage/

# What plant-follow.php saves before it breaks a file on purpose. It restores
# from this, so a stray one means a planted fault is still in the working tree.
.follow-original.bak

# A generic header image dropped in the project root for an email mock-up. It
# is not part of the plugin: the mail banner is SFAF_Email::banner_url(), which
# resolves a URL from settings, and nothing in the tree reads this file.
SFAF-generic-header-skyline-1200x212.png
